<!--
  The split-pane indicator, right pane active.

  # Where this came from, which is not Material Symbols

  **Derived from a screenshot of agterm's own toolbar**, taken by the owner on 2026-08-25 and measured
  pixel by pixel rather than eyeballed. That provenance is the point: he recognises this picture from
  his laptop, and the phone showing him the same one is most of its value: agterm draws a small
  indicator of the panes with the active one lit, and this is that picture.

  What the measurement gave, from the 30x23px original:

    box              30 wide x 23 high      -> 880 x 675 here, the same 1.30 ratio
    border           2/30 of the width      -> 60
    the active half  exactly half the width -> the hole starts at the midpoint, 480
    corner radius    ~3px                   -> 90 outer, 30 on the hole

  # Solid against hollow, never two shades

  The right half is SOLID and the left half is a HOLE — presence against absence, not light grey
  against dark grey. That is the same property the owner asked for when he turned down a tinted label
  and asked for a checkmark, and it is why this reads at 18dp when a shading difference would not.

  `evenOdd` is what makes the second subpath a hole rather than a second shape: the hole is
  TRANSPARENT, so it shows whatever is behind the icon and takes no tint. A hole painted in a
  background colour would be a lie on any surface but the one it was picked for.

  # Coordinates are plain, not Material's negative-Y

  The converted glyphs in this directory carry a `<group android:translateY="960">` because they came
  from SVGs on a `0 -960 960 960` viewBox. Nothing was converted here, so there is no offset to undo.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="960"
    android:viewportHeight="960">
    <path
        android:fillColor="@android:color/white"
        android:fillType="evenOdd"
        android:pathData="M130,142 L830,142 A90,90 0 0 1 920,232 L920,727 A90,90 0 0 1 830,817 L130,817 A90,90 0 0 1 40,727 L40,232 A90,90 0 0 1 130,142 Z M130,202 L450,202 A30,30 0 0 1 480,232 L480,727 A30,30 0 0 1 450,757 L130,757 A30,30 0 0 1 100,727 L100,232 A30,30 0 0 1 130,202 Z" />
</vector>
